.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Intermediate image dumps and any derived imagery are patient-derived data.
# Never commit them.
#
# data/out/ additionally holds, as of Phase 3, the extraction cache
# (data/out/extract_cache/, keyed per spec section 3.5 on the crop image hash,
# region, model and prompt version), the per-page extraction results
# (data/out/extract/) and the vitals accuracy metrics
# (phase3_vitals_metrics.json). All three record a real patient's observations --
# weight, temperature, SpO2, heart rate -- and the raw model reply about them, so
# they are PHI exactly as much as data/dumps/ and data/segments/ are. Filenames
# are content hashes or page_ids only, never a source filename, but the whole
# tree is excluded regardless.
#
# Phase 4 adds three more things to the same tree, and they are MORE sensitive
# than Phase 3's, not less: data/out/extract_agreement/ (both passes' readings of
# every region, side by side), the per-page extraction results for the header and
# prescription regions -- which now include the patient's NAME, ID and medication
# list, not just their vitals -- and phase4_extract_metrics.json, which embeds the
# ground truth it scored against. Same rule, no exceptions.
data/dumps/
data/out/

# Phase 2 region and prescription-line crops (python -m src.segment run
# --dump-crops). These are crops of real scans -- the header strip crop is a
# patient's name and ID, the vitals crop is their observations -- so they are
# PHI exactly as much as data/dumps/ is. The per-page manifest.json alongside
# them is keyed on the content-hash page_id and holds no filename, but it lives
# in the same tree, so the whole tree is excluded.
data/segments/

# Letterhead templates (config/templates/). The private working repo keeps
# these: crops of the clinic's printed letterhead, used for anchoring. They
# identify the clinic and the doctor, so this public copy leaves them out.
# Regenerate your own with `python -m src.segment make-templates`.
config/templates/

# Real scans are PHI. Never commit them.
samples/

# Ground-truth fixtures record the PATH of their source scan, and those
# filenames contain real patient names -- so fixtures are PHI too. (Verified:
# all 7 current fixtures contain a patient-name token.) The fixture *format*
# is documented in src/eval/fixtures.py; the filled-in fixtures never leave
# the operator's machine.
data/fixtures/

# Scratch/probe output. Not part of the deliverable.
tmp_probe/

# Local, machine-specific Claude Code permission settings.
.claude/settings.local.json
